  "prefLabel": "Man 208.10 Failure to Attend Hearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Man 208.10 Failure to Attend Hearing. If any party to whom notice has been given in accordance with Man 208.03 fails to attend a hearing, the presiding officer shall declare that party to be in default and shall either:\n\n(a) Dismiss the case, if the party with the burden of proof fails to appear; or\n\n(b) Rule that the board hear the testimony and receive the evidence offered by a party, if that party has the burden of proof in the case and issue a decision on the merits.\n\nSource. #8286-A, eff 2-16-05",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/man100-400.html"
